---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SwimProgression from "../components/SwimProgression.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Griffin Thomas. Aerospace engineering student at Arizona State, planespotter, and breaststroke swimmer."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[88rem]">
    <section>
      <p class="data">Tempe, Arizona / West Seattle, Washington</p>
      <h1 class="font-display mt-5 text-4xl sm:text-6xl">About</h1>

      <div class="measure text-graphite mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          I study aerospace engineering at Arizona State, in the Aeronautics concentration.
          I grew up in West Seattle and went to high school in Exeter, New Hampshire.
          I&rsquo;m back in the Pacific Northwest every summer.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most of what I do is build things and then find out what&rsquo;s wrong with them.
          At the moment that&rsquo;s a 59-inch MQ-9-style airframe printed in modular
          sections, so a broken part can be reprinted without starting the whole aircraft
          over. Wings, tail and electronics are all done. It has never flown, because I
          left the control surfaces until last and never finished them.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also run a Raspberry Pi and an RTL-SDR that decodes 1090 MHz transponder data
          and feeds FlightRadar24 as T-KBFI187. Its range is worse than it should be. The
          antenna is the next thing to fix.
        </p>
        <p>
          I shoot aircraft at Sea-Tac, Boeing Field, and Sky Harbor on a Canon Rebel T7,
          usually with a 75-300. I swim breaststroke, and I guard at Normandy Park Swim
          Club outside Seattle.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <SwimProgression />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
